    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d23">

                <pb facs="0037" n="23" sameAs="frus:frus1949v07p1/pg23"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">851G.01/5–749:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-05-07T17:00:00+01:00">May 7, 1949—5 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1862. While Embassy has not received copy Department’s 70, May 2, to
                        Saigon,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d23-f1"/> I wish to state my concurrence in
                    general line contained latter’s 1412 [<hi rendition="#italic">141</hi>], May 6,
                    to Department.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d23-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>In connection with Abbott’s recommendation for “immediate and continued pressure”
                    (Paragraph 4–<hi rendition="#italic">a</hi>), in which I expressly concur, I
                    suggest that in immediate stage it would be helpful, in event Embassy is to
                    undertake such representations, if they could be accompanied by indications our
                    intentions according <hi rendition="#italic">b</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >c</hi>, and possible <hi rendition="#italic">d</hi>, same paragraph,
                    provided representations are successful.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 1862 (for action); repeated Saigon 73 (for information).</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d23-f1" n="1" xml:id="d23-f1-content">
                <p>The Department repeated telegram 70 in telegram 1522, May 10, 8 p. m., to
                    Paris.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d23-f2" n="2" xml:id="d23-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
